    introTranscript: "Most divisions describe their culture in the language of intention: we value different perspectives, we support each other, everyone belongs here. Staff read those statements against something else entirely. They read them against the posting that required a credential the work never needed, the panel of three people from the same unit, the first month where nobody said what good looked like, the stretch assignment that went to somebody else, and the accommodation request that disappeared for six weeks. This module treats team culture as the sum of those decisions rather than as a mood. It looks at how a job is posted and filled, what the first weeks teach people, how work and supervision time get handed out, and who is quietly asked to do unpaid work because of who they are. It ends with a barrier review you can run on one workforce process in about six hours, and a first fix that needs nobody's permission.",
